## Diagram Type Selection

Choose the single most appropriate diagram type. Not everything is a flowchart.

| If the target is... | Use | Because |
|---|---|---|
| SQL schema files, CREATE TABLE statements, database entities | **erd** | Crow's Foot shows cardinality directly |
| A function's control flow, decision tree, template cascade, pipeline | **flowchart** | Branches and paths are first-class |
| An enum with lifecycle variants, state machine, status transitions | **state** | States and transitions are the domain, not an overlay |
| Message passing, request/response chains, event propagation across services | **sequence** | Participants and message ordering are explicit |
| Traits, structs, impl blocks — type hierarchies and composition | **class** | Inheritance and composition have dedicated UML syntax |
| System topology, service boundaries, deployment architecture, data flow between services | **architecture** | Services, junctions, and ports model deployment shape |
| Module boundaries, component composition, nested block structure | **block** | Columns/rows and nested blocks model structural decomposition |
| Multi-dimensional capability assessment, metric profiles, comparative scoring | **radar** | Axes show per-dimension strength; curves compare entities |
| Hierarchical quantity data, code-size-by-module, budget allocation, directory proportions | **treemap** | Nested rectangles encode quantity as area |
| Weighted flow between stages — process, pipeline, budget, funnel, user journey | **sankey** | Edge width encodes flow magnitude; staged flow is first-class |
| Task board, work items grouped by status, kata-kanban snapshots | **kanban** | Columns are statuses; tasks are cards with metadata |
| Scheduled work, milestones, project timeline, phase dependencies | **gantt** | Time axis with bars shows duration and ordering |
| Proportional breakdown, categorical distribution, market share | **pie** | Slices show parts of a whole |
| Commit history, branch structure, merge/fork events in a repository | **gitgraph** | Branches and commits model version-control topology |
| Hierarchical concept maps, taxonomy, org structure, idea decomposition | **mindmap** | Radial nesting shows parent-child relationships |
| Chronological events, project phases, release history, biographical timeline | **timeline** | Time-ordered events with optional per-event metadata |
| 2×2 strategic matrix, Wardley map, prioritization grid, scenario quadrants | **quadrant** | Two-axis placement reveals strategic positioning |
| Quantitative x-y data, performance curves, benchmarks, metric trends | **xychart** | Cartesian axes plot numeric series |
| User journey, experience mapping, satisfaction stages | **journey** | Ordered stages with sentiment scores |

**Heuristics:** If you see states named like Pending/Active/Completed → use state. If you see arrows between services with messages → use sequence. If you see boxes with true/false branches → use flowchart. If you see CREATE TABLE → use erd. If you see service boundaries and deployment topology → use architecture. If you see weighted flow with quantities → use sankey. If you see a task board with status columns → use kanban. If you see hierarchical quantities (size per module) → use treemap. If you see multi-axis capability scoring → use radar.

## Diataxis Quadrant

Classify which quadrant the diagram will serve:

| Quadrant | Reader is... | Diagram should... |
|---|---|---|
| **reference** | Consulting facts | Be austere, complete, mirror code structure |
| **explanation** | Reflecting on design | Show relationships, context, trade-offs |
| **how-to** | Executing a task | Show the path, stay focused on the goal |
| **tutorial** | Following a lesson | Be minimal, point out what to notice |

Default to **reference** unless the user's intent suggests otherwise.

## Output

Return a JSON object:

```json
{
  "diagram_type": "erd | flowchart | state | sequence | class | architecture | block | radar | treemap | sankey | kanban | gantt | pie | gitgraph | mindmap | timeline | quadrant | xychart | journey",
  "diataxis_quadrant": "reference | explanation | how-to | tutorial",
  "source_files": ["path/to/schema.sql", ...],
  "rationale": "One sentence explaining why this type and quadrant were chosen."
}
```
